      "category": "pycore_pystate",
      "signature": "_PyThreadState_GET()",
      "params": [],
      "returnType": "PyThreadState*",
      "docs": "Get the current Python thread state.\nEfficient macro reading directly the 'gilstate.tstate_current' atomic\nvariable. The macro is unsafe: it does not check for error and it can\nreturn NULL.\nThe caller must hold the GIL.\nSee also PyThreadState_Get() and _PyThreadState_UncheckedGet()."
